  m_Name: Object_11
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  partName: Exhaust Manifold Stud
  description: The Exhaust Manifold Stud is a tiny, elongated component positioned
    at the top-center-front of the engine, fabricated from Material.001, and plays
    a vital role in securing the exhaust manifold to the engine block. Its primary
    function is to withstand the high temperatures and stresses associated with exhaust
    gas flow, and its material composition is chosen for its ability to resist thermal
    degradation. Interestingly, the Exhaust Manifold Stud is often coated with a
    specialized layer to enhance its corrosion resistance and extend its service
    life.
  audioExplanation: {fileID: 0}
